(559691, 55972, 7252, '<td valign="top">I''ve looked at this image several times now and I must say I just don''t get it. Is it really a road sign? What does the "End of Hell" signify to the motorist?</td>', 'I''ve looked at this image several times now and I must say I just don''t get it. Is it really a road sign? What does the "End of Hell" signify to the motorist?', '2004-01-27 23:30:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(559693, 55773, 12160, '<td valign="top">I had to look a second time at this photo which is very beautiful indeed. The colors are wonderful and the image is sharp. I like the perspective and the leading lines. The road sign though is small (no entry) but the 50% sign is more prevalent because of it''s size... i don''t think that it qualifies as a road sign. Looking at this makes me think that the woman in red is the subject of the photo. Overall, it''s a really nice image. I gave you a 7 but i''m bumping it to 8. Good luck!</td>', 'I had to look a second time at this photo which is very beautiful indeed. The colors are wonderful and the image is sharp. I like the perspective and the leading lines. The road sign though is small (no entry) but the 50% sign is more prevalent because of it''s size... i don''t think that it qualifies as a road sign. Looking at this makes me think that the woman in red is the subject of the photo. Overall, it''s a really nice image. I gave you a 7 but i''m bumping it to 8. Good luck!', '2004-01-27 23:31:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(559696, 55978, 7252, '<td valign="top">I don''t know if it happened in camera or in post but this is seriously over-saturated. Looks like what ever smoothing action or program you''ve used has also made the edges of the sign go completely fuzzy. Compositionally there just isn''t much here. A straightforward shot of the sign from what appears to be from a typical adult viewpoint. The sign itself is certainly something you don''t see every day. A more interesting angle, perhaps showing some of the surroundings, would improve the shot as well as reducing the over done processing.</td>', 'I don''t know if it happened in camera or in post but this is seriously over-saturated. Looks like what ever smoothing action or program you''ve used has also made the edges of the sign go completely fuzzy. Compositionally there just isn''t much here. A straightforward shot of the sign from what appears to be from a typical adult viewpoint. The sign itself is certainly something you don''t see every day. A more interesting angle, perhaps showing some of the surroundings, would improve the shot as well as reducing the over done processing.', '2004-01-27 23:34:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(559698, 56108, 7252, '<td valign="top">This is much too grainy, soft, and bland in composition. Was digital zoom used? If so I would avoid that in future shots. High ISO? If so I would use the lowest ISO your camera has and use a tripod to reduce noise to the lowest possible levels for your camera. I would also try to find something unique in either the setting or the sign itself and try to more clearly show that or those elements you found interesting.</td>', 'This is much too grainy, soft, and bland in composition. Was digital zoom used? If so I would avoid that in future shots. High ISO? If so I would use the lowest ISO your camera has and use a tripod to reduce noise to the lowest possible levels for your camera. I would also try to find something unique in either the setting or the sign itself and try to more clearly show that or those elements you found interesting.', '2004-01-27 23:37:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(559699, 55613, 15407, '<td valign="top">My Home!  I was born here!</td>', 'My Home!  I was born here!', '2004-01-27 23:38:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(559703, 55958, 7252, '<td valign="top">While I like the idea the execution could be a little better. The main problem is the over exposure of the signs. A shorter flash duration might help there. It''s hard to say because they are so reflective. A slight bump in contrast and some sharpening should help bring out the signs as well. Perhaps an even longer shutter to get more of the "crazy" lights would increase interest as well. As I said a very solid concept. I wouldn''t hesitate to keep at this.</td>', 'While I like the idea the execution could be a little better. The main problem is the over exposure of the signs. A shorter flash duration might help there. It''s hard to say because they are so reflective. A slight bump in contrast and some sharpening should help bring out the signs as well. Perhaps an even longer shutter to get more of the "crazy" lights would increase interest as well. As I said a very solid concept. I wouldn''t hesitate to keep at this.', '2004-01-27 23:40:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(559705, 56005, 15407, '<td valign="top">I can''t even do it on two!</td>', 'I can''t even do it on two!', '2004-01-27 23:43:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(559707, 55768, 15407, '<td valign="top">Wonder Why?</td>', 'Wonder Why?', '2004-01-27 23:45:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(559711, 55962, 7252, '<td valign="top">I''ve waffled on this for some time now. While I think you make a very strong statement with this photo, in the end I think I must vote for the spirit of the challenge. As such I don''t think this image meets the challenge because there isn''t a road sign. As for the photo itself I very much like the concept. I have two minor issues though. First is the relatively shallow DOF. I would prefer a tighter aperture and the same level of sharpness in the fore and backgrounds. The second issue is the strong line of the pole and the building mirror each other and are too close. If you came around slightly to the right you could have both virticles but the added distance between them I think would make the image overall stronger.  Have you considered a B&amp;W version? It seems it like it would be appropriate for this type of image.</td>', 'I''ve waffled on this for some time now. While I think you make a very strong statement with this photo, in the end I think I must vote for the spirit of the challenge. As such I don''t think this image meets the challenge because there isn''t a road sign. As for the photo itself I very much like the concept. I have two minor issues though. First is the relatively shallow DOF. I would prefer a tighter aperture and the same level of sharpness in the fore and backgrounds. The second issue is the strong line of the pole and the building mirror each other and are too close. If you came around slightly to the right you could have both virticles but the added distance between them I think would make the image overall stronger.  Have you considered a B&W version? It seems it like it would be appropriate for this type of image.', '2004-01-27 23:49:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(559713, 56122, 7252, '<td valign="top">Clear and bright but just a tad too tight in the crop. A little more room on the left and bottom would be nice.</td>', 'Clear and bright but just a tad too tight in the crop. A little more room on the left and bottom would be nice.', '2004-01-27 23:51:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(559715, 55749, 7252, '<td valign="top">It took me ages to figure out what you meant. Of course once I did it becomes all too obvious. The photo is nice and sharp but I think a little dark behind the clubs. I think also that removing the dirt and scratch marks would improve the photo. Creative and clever though.</td>', 'It took me ages to figure out what you meant. Of course once I did it becomes all too obvious. The photo is nice and sharp but I think a little dark behind the clubs. I think also that removing the dirt and scratch marks would improve the photo. Creative and clever though.', '2004-01-27 23:56:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(559716, 55324, 7252, '<td valign="top">One must ask oneself why on earth doesn''t this person have his lights on??? He must be one of my fellow Californians. As a group we don''t have the road sense of an opossum. (Which are found dead on the road around here all the time)</td>', 'One must ask oneself why on earth doesn''t this person have his lights on??? He must be one of my fellow Californians. As a group we don''t have the road sense of an opossum. (Which are found dead on the road around here all the time)', '2004-01-27 23:59:38.000000', NULL, 1),
